Q: Default value if variable not sets A: <p>Starting with PHP 7.4 you can use <a href="https://wiki.php.net/rfc/null_coalesce_equal_operator" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Null Coalescing Assignment Operator (php.net)</a>:</p>
<p>In your code example:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>if (($p ??= &quot;&quot;) == &quot;a&quot;) doSomething();
</code></pre>
<p>If <code>$p</code> is <code>null</code> or <code>unset</code> then it's value sets to <code>&quot;&quot;</code> (empty string). This is equals to:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>$p = (isset($p) &amp;&amp; !is_null($p) ? $p : &quot;&quot;);
if ($p == &quot;a&quot;) doSomething();
</code></pre>
<p>or to</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>$p ??= &quot;&quot;;
if ($p == &quot;a&quot;) doSomething();
</code></pre>
<p>Example from docs:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>// The folloving lines are doing the same
$this-&gt;request-&gt;data['comments']['user_id'] = $this-&gt;request-&gt;data['comments']['user_id'] ?? 'value';
// Instead of repeating variables with long names, the equal coalesce operator is used
$this-&gt;request-&gt;data['comments']['user_id'] ??= 'value';
</code></pre>
<p>Discussion and more examples:</p>
<p><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/59102708/what-is-null-coalescing-assignment-operator-in-php-7-4">What is null coalescing assignment ??= operator in PHP 7.4 (stackoverflow.com)</a></p>

Q: Typescript adding types to EventEmitter A: <p>I use that way for build a EventEmitter class with type guards, hope that will help some one.</p>
<pre><code>import EventEmitter from 'node:events';

type BaseEventTable = Record&lt;string, unknown[]&gt;;

/**
 * Transform an interface with array properties into an event table,
 * where keys are event names and values are the argument types
 * for the event listeners.
 */
type InterfaceToEventTable&lt;T extends object&gt; = {
  [K in keyof T]: T[K] extends unknown[] ? T[K] : never;
};

type GetEventNameFromEventTable&lt;EventTable extends BaseEventTable, K = keyof EventTable&gt; = Exclude&lt;K, number&gt;;

class TypeEventEmitter&lt;
  RawEventTable extends object,
  EventTable extends InterfaceToEventTable&lt;RawEventTable&gt; = InterfaceToEventTable&lt;RawEventTable&gt;,
  EventName extends GetEventNameFromEventTable&lt;EventTable&gt; = GetEventNameFromEventTable&lt;EventTable&gt;
&gt; extends EventEmitter {
  override on&lt;CurrentEventName extends EventName&gt;(
    eventName: CurrentEventName,
    listener: (...args: EventTable[CurrentEventName]) =&gt; void
  ): this {
    return super.on(eventName, listener);
  }

  override once&lt;CurrentEventName extends EventName&gt;(
    eventName: CurrentEventName,
    listener: (...args: EventTable[CurrentEventName]) =&gt; void
  ): this {
    return super.once(eventName, listener);
  }

  override emit&lt;CurrentEventName extends EventName&gt;(
    eventName: CurrentEventName,
    ...args: EventTable[CurrentEventName]
  ): boolean {
    return super.emit(eventName, ...args);
  }

  override off&lt;CurrentEventName extends EventName&gt;(
    eventName: CurrentEventName,
    listener: (...args: EventTable[CurrentEventName]) =&gt; void
  ): this {
    return super.off(eventName, listener);
  }

  override removeListener&lt;CurrentEventName extends EventName&gt;(
    eventName: CurrentEventName,
    listener: (...args: EventTable[CurrentEventName]) =&gt; void
  ): this {
    return super.removeListener(eventName, listener);
  }
}

export { TypeEventEmitter };
</code></pre>
